 {:status :proposal-for-the-distinct-offline-source-grant-not-implemented
  :version "oikos.dispatch/v1"
  :framing {:prefix :four-byte-unsigned-big-endian-body-length
            :body-min-bytes 2 :body-max-bytes 65536 :frame-max-bytes 65540
            :messages-per-input 1
            :rule "Exact-length UTF-8 JSON object; reject truncation, trailing bytes/second messages, BOM, invalid UTF-8 and unknown framing. These are in-memory frame tests, not claims about a live stream."}
  :decode-bounds {:max-depth 12 :max-value-nodes 4096 :max-decoded-string-utf8-bytes 8192
                  :max-container-members 128 :max-object-key-utf8-bytes 64
                  :max-integer 9007199254740991}
  :decode-law "Reject duplicate keys at every nesting depth BEFORE any parser can collapse them; bounded structural scanning/decoding, not regex duplicate guessing or JSON.parse alone. Reject non-scalar Unicode/unpaired surrogate escapes, nulls where disallowed, fractions/exponents, negative/negative-zero/inexact numbers and noncanonical numeric spellings. Map only fixed schema field/operation literals; never intern arbitrary client strings as keywords or use tagged/Lisp readers."
  :closed-request-fields ["protocol-version" "request-id" "contract-version" "contract-digest"
                          "named-request" "approval-reference"]
  :request-law "All six keys required, no extras. Protocol/version/digest equal frozen pins. request-id is canonical lowercase UUID; named-request maps only the existing frozen closed request fields and four operation enums and must pass the unchanged frozen request schema. approval-reference is null for reads and a canonical lowercase UUID reference for mutations, never an authority-bearing approval payload. No client endpoint, executable, wrapper/function, raw eval/IPC, scope, resource facts or approval-context map."
  :frozen-semantic-bounds {:range-bytes 4096 :replacement-utf8-bytes 4096 :resulting-buffer-utf8-bytes 1048576}
  :bound-rule "Framing/JSON escaping never changes the frozen decoded byte bounds; escaped controls/quotes/backslashes/newlines and Lisp-looking literal text are data. A codec cannot prove actual native text boundaries or current buffer length. Preserve canonical text without normalization/newline conversion."
  :offline-results {:invalid-input {:status :denied :code :dispatch-input-refused :authority :none}
                    :runtime-attempt {:status :denied :code :dispatcher-unavailable :authority :none}
                    :valid-codec :inert-decoded-or-encoded-value-with-authority-none-only}
  :diagnostics "Constant input-free refusals; no raw exception/cause, rejected payload, replacement text, linkable resource/approval IDs or frame content in logs. New outer result laws do not change cap/satisfied or relabel it authorized/applied. Runtime applied/read/indeterminate response schemas remain part of separately reviewed real consumer/handler protocol, not evidence from offline tests."
